# CI-Spellbook environment. Copy to `.env` and uncomment what you need.
# Everything here is optional; the app runs with none of it set.
#
# See docs/operations/error-reporting.md.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Error reporting (Sentry) — opt-in, OFF by default.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BUILD TIME. Vite bakes VITE_* into the bundle, so these must be set when
# `npm run build` runs — setting them on a running container does nothing.
# With VITE_SENTRY_DSN unset the whole Sentry SDK is tree-shaken out of the
# bundle, so the app cannot phone home at all.
#
# For the container image, pass them as build args instead:
#   docker build --build-arg VITE_SENTRY_DSN=... .
#
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://<key>@o<org>.ingest.us.sentry.io/<id>
# VITE_SENTRY_RELEASE=ci-spellbook@1.1.0
# VITE_CI_ENVIRONMENT=production

# RUNTIME kill switches. Read by whatever serves the bundle (the nginx
# entrypoint in the image, the Vite dev/preview server locally) and handed to
# the browser at /api/config/telemetry, so they can turn reporting off without
# rebuilding an image that has a DSN baked in. Precedence:
# CI_LOCAL_ONLY > CI_TELEMETRY > the DSN.
#
# CI_TELEMETRY=off      # also: false, 0, no, disabled
# CI_LOCAL_ONLY=true    # local-only mode means zero phone-home
